      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Generational indoctrination into the belief that the Low-Tiers are biologically predisposed to unruliness and thereby less \"human\" indeed leads to a moral detachment among the High-Tiers. They absolve themselves of guilt and view their harsh laws as not only justified but also a necessary societal function to maintain order and protect their own evolutionary and civilized nature.\n\nThis mindset cultivates a remarkable superiority complex among the High-Tiers, who regard themselves as more enlightened or advanced beings within the same species—so to speak. They differentiate themselves as a \"higher\" subspecies who must preserve humanity's progress and rationality by managing the supposedly \"primitive\" Low-Tiers. To them, the Low-Tiers represent a stage of regression that the High-Tiers have advanced beyond, and it is their duty to wield their biological advantage to ensure that societal standards and civilization remain uncontaminated by these instinctual forces. Effectively, they adopt a paternalistic philosophy that their own refined nature bestows upon them a more genuine human identity.",
      "source": "target",
